It is late morning.
I take my backpack and walk to the park.
There is a large flea market there today.
Flea markets are always very bustling on Sundays in Berlin.
I slowly stroll around between the tables.
I often come here.
Sometimes I just look.
I stop at a clothing stall.
The vendor looks at me.
"Would you like to see that jacket?" he asks.
He points to a dark jacket right at the back.
I smile and politely correct him.
"No, thank you," I answer.
"I do not want that jacket."
I point to a light summer jacket right in front of me.
"I want to look at this jacket."
"Ah, a good choice," the vendor says.
"This jacket is perfect for the weather today."
He hands me the jacket across the table.
